{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Spider Bomb and Firepot Drone travel to their target and explode (#5291, #5292, #4386)",
  "contract": [
    "Build: Spider Bomb 500535 reads 'Build a Spider Bomb that will immediately run towards your target and",
    "detonate', and Build: Firepot Drone 500600 reads that the drone 'flies towards your target, dropping a",
    "bomb along its path and exploding upon landing'. AscensionDB (Exiles DB) lists Spider Bomb Explosion",
    "801982 as cast by NPC 226012. Both builds summon a device (Spider Bomb 226012 at DEST_CASTER_RANDOM",
    "within 6 yd, Firepot Drone 226112 at DEST_CASTER_FRONT 3 yd) that lives 15 s and runs",
    "npc_ascension_tinker_device, which explodes once the device is within 2 yd of its focus. The golem",
    "stands 20 yd in front of the Tinker with passive fixture reaction, so only a device that travels to it",
    "can damage it. #5291/#5292/#4386 report that both devices stand still and never explode;",
    "ChaseMovementGenerator pauses whenever the chaser's victim is not the chase target, and the passive",
    "device never attacks. Each device must reach the golem, damage it and be gone well before its 15 s",
    "duration. The fixture creatures do not regenerate health. Each of eight ordinary builds per device must",
    "produce a native detonation spell-go packet from the summoned entry and disappear before its original",
    "fifteen-second lifetime. Native equal-level NPC explosions retain their authored hit rolls (4% magic",
    "miss for Spider Bomb, 5% ranged miss for Firepot), so damage is required across eight eligible",
    "detonations for each device instead of demanding a hit from one roll: the probability of eight misses is",
    "at most 0.05^8 < 4e-11. Actual detonation packets and timely disappearance prove arrival even when a",
    "damage roll misses. Refill Mana, reset the parent build cooldown, and restore Firepot's three native",
    "charges (SpellCharges category 124, ten-second recharge) between independent trials; do not modify",
    "explosion hit chance or cost handling."
  ],
